hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1592","We have Zakaria bin Yahya bin Aban, we have Amr bin Al-Rabi’ bin Tariq, we have Ikrimah bin Ibrahim, we have Saeed bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, Anas bin Malik told me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “While I was between the corner and the place, I heard him say: Someone to talk to him,” so he mentioned the hadith of the Ascension in its entirety, and said: “Then it was announced that you will have ten prayers for every prayer.” He said: “So I landed, and when the sun had set, In the middle of the sky, Gabriel descended in a row of angels, led him in prayer, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered his companions, so they lined up behind him, so they continued. Through Gabriel, and the Companions of the Prophet were led by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he led them in prayer four times, fearing the recitation, then he left them, until it was corrected. When the sun was pure white, Gabriel descended and led them in prayer for four times, during which the recitation was difficult, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed with Gabriel. The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he left them, until when the sun had set, Gabriel came down and prayed. He recited them three times, reciting aloud in two rak’ahs, and reciting the prayer in one. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entrusted himself to Gabriel, and the Companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entrusted themselves to Gabriel. He greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When twilight set, Gabriel descended and led them in four rak’ahs of prayer: he would recite out loud in two rak’ahs, and silently in two. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entrusted himself to Gabriel, and the Companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entrusted themselves to the Prophet, peace be upon him, so they spent the night until the morning came down. Gabriel led them in two rak’ahs, prolonging the recitation.” Abu Bakr said: This news was narrated by the Basrans, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Malik ibn Sa`sa’ah, the story of the ascension, And they said at the end of it, Al-Hasan said: “When the sun had set, Gabriel descended,” and at the end of it, he made the news from this place in the leadership of Gabriel a messenger, On the authority of Al-Hasan and Ikrimah bin Ibrahim, this story was included in the story of Anas bin Malik. This story is not recorded on the authority of Anas, except that the people of the Qiblah did not disagree that everything that was mentioned in this report was clearly stated. And the fear of recitation during prayer, as mentioned in this report."
